#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# matrix_power

#% text
# `matrix_power(m, k)` gives the k-th power of a square matrix.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Integer powers by repeated squaring; negative powers through the inverse; other powers as the matrix function x^k.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
matrix_power([[1, 1], [1, 0]], 10)
#% output
#= [[89, 55], [55, 34]]

#% cell
matrix_power([[1, 2], [3, 4]], -1)
#% output
#= [[-2, 1], [3/2, -1/2]]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
matrix_power([[2, 1], [1, 2]], 1/2)
#% output
#= [[(1/2)*(1 + 3^(1/2)), (1/2)*(-1 + 3^(1/2))], [(1/2)*(-1 + 3^(1/2)), (1/2)*(1 + 3^(1/2))]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `matrix_function`, `dot`, `inverse`
